**Critical rules:**
- Column names must match exactly — trailing spaces cause null values
- `Client ID` cannot be duplicated in the header
- Save source file as UTF-8 before upload — Windows-1252 encoding produces garbled characters in NocoDB
- Blank `Raw Text` is valid — GPT handles star-only records with placeholder text

**Note added this cycle:** this exact class of encoding bug — a source file saved in the wrong encoding producing garbled characters in NocoDB — is what caused the EIP Spanish dictionary corruption resolved this cycle (see Open Items #3). The warning above isn't theoretical; it's a confirmed failure mode.

