### NORMALIZATION (Steps 4–9)

**Step 4 - CSV Parse**
Maps CSV columns to pipeline fields. Runs once for all items before SplitInBatches.

```javascript
const items = $input.all();
const batchId = `BATCH-${Date.now()}`;
const batchStartTime = new Date().toISOString();
const expectedCount = items.length;
return items.map(item => ({
  json: {
    date: item.json['Date'] || item.json['\uFEFFDate'] || '',
    platform: item.json['Platform'] || '',
    raw_text: item.json['Raw Text'] || '',
    reviewer_name: item.json['Reviewer Name'] || null,
    lang_csv: (item.json['Lang'] || item.json['lang'] || '').toLowerCase() || null,
    star_rating: item.json['Stars rating'] ? Number(item.json['Stars rating']) : null,
    client_id: item.json['Client ID'] || null,
    batch_id: batchId,
    batch_start_time: batchStartTime,
    expected_count: expectedCount
  }
}));
```

**Key rules:**
- `Stars rating` — exact column name including space and lowercase r
- `lang_csv` reads both `Lang` and `lang` defensively — handles either casing
- `star_rating` cast to Number — null if absent
- BOM character (`\uFEFF`) handled on Date field

